    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "The comments for sql (at least postgres) is `--`, but when I try to do `comment line`, `comment visual` or any other, I get this message `(mini.comment) Option 'commentstring' is empty.` and nothing happens. Using `LazyNvim` default settings, this might be vim specific, but I have no idea what to set",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">The comments for sql (at least postgres) is <code class=\"notranslate\">--</code>, but when I try to do <code class=\"notranslate\">comment line</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">comment visual</code> or any other, I get this message <code class=\"notranslate\">(mini.comment) Option 'commentstring' is empty.</code> and nothing happens. Using <code class=\"notranslate\">LazyNvim</code> default settings, this might be vim specific, but I have no idea what to set</p>",
    "bodyText": "The comments for sql (at least postgres) is --, but when I try to do comment line, comment visual or any other, I get this message (mini.comment) Option 'commentstring' is empty. and nothing happens. Using LazyNvim default settings, this might be vim specific, but I have no idea what to set",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
