                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Hi! Thank you for the tip, I've also started using it.\r\n\r\n@echasnovski just wanted to clarify, do you think it is expected behaviour of the plugin? I think it would be great if mini.comment supported SQL files out of the box.\r\n\r\nIt would also be great if the warning from the plugin was more verbose. Also it would be great if README had a troubleshooting section related to that.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi! Thank you for the tip, I've also started using it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> just wanted to clarify, do you think it is expected behaviour of the plugin? I think it would be great if mini.comment supported SQL files out of the box.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It would also be great if the warning from the plugin was more verbose. Also it would be great if README had a troubleshooting section related to that.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Hi! Thank you for the tip, I've also started using it.\n@echasnovski just wanted to clarify, do you think it is expected behaviour of the plugin? I think it would be great if mini.comment supported SQL files out of the box.\nIt would also be great if the warning from the plugin was more verbose. Also it would be great if README had a troubleshooting section related to that.",
