                },
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yes, not working if 'commentstring' is not available is a completely expected behavior. 'mini.comment' [uses this option](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/df1559e2ed7ece458e0a97a8bb9556d465d1c775/doc/mini-comment.txt#L11-L14) to infer the structure of how it should comment/uncomment lines.\r\n\r\n> It would also be great if the warning from the plugin was more verbose. Also it would be great if README had a troubleshooting section related to that.\r\n\r\nWhat wording would help you in this particular case? My expectation is that 'mini.comment' is used with at least prior knowledge of what Neovim options are and how to set them. There is a note that present 'commentstring' is essential for 'mini.comment', so the wording of \"Option 'commentstring' is empty\" seemed OK to me at the time.\r\n\r\n**Edit**: on Nightly (the future 0.11) this is already solved as on [2024-05-18 the 'commentstring' option](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/b7e896671500a6e9a0c773bc6bac2d073e588eba/runtime/ftplugin/sql.vim#L7) is now automatically set. I also checked this on latest Nightly.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, not working if 'commentstring' is not available is a completely expected behavior. 'mini.comment' <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/df1559e2ed7ece458e0a97a8bb9556d465d1c775/doc/mini-comment.txt#L11-L14\">uses this option</a> to infer the structure of how it should comment/uncomment lines.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It would also be great if the warning from the plugin was more verbose. Also it would be great if README had a troubleshooting section related to that.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What wording would help you in this particular case? My expectation is that 'mini.comment' is used with at least prior knowledge of what Neovim options are and how to set them. There is a note that present 'commentstring' is essential for 'mini.comment', so the wording of \"Option 'commentstring' is empty\" seemed OK to me at the time.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Edit</strong>: on Nightly (the future 0.11) this is already solved as on <a href=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/b7e896671500a6e9a0c773bc6bac2d073e588eba/runtime/ftplugin/sql.vim#L7\">2024-05-18 the 'commentstring' option</a> is now automatically set. I also checked this on latest Nightly.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, not working if 'commentstring' is not available is a completely expected behavior. 'mini.comment' uses this option to infer the structure of how it should comment/uncomment lines.\n\nIt would also be great if the warning from the plugin was more verbose. Also it would be great if README had a troubleshooting section related to that.\n\nWhat wording would help you in this particular case? My expectation is that 'mini.comment' is used with at least prior knowledge of what Neovim options are and how to set them. There is a note that present 'commentstring' is essential for 'mini.comment', so the wording of \"Option 'commentstring' is empty\" seemed OK to me at the time.\nEdit: on Nightly (the future 0.11) this is already solved as on 2024-05-18 the 'commentstring' option is now automatically set. I also checked this on latest Nightly.",
