                },
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3424811?u=82f36ee3c722610815d33aba4bcae31212bd0171&v=4",
                        "login": "biozz",
                        "resourcePath": "/biozz",
                        "url": "https://github.com/biozz"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "> What wording would help you in this particular case?\r\n\r\nI would just put your previous answer into the readme or help text section you linked. Because it is clear and straight to the point.\r\n\r\n```\r\n- Comment structure by default is inferred from 'commentstring': either\r\n  from current buffer or from locally active tree-sitter language (only on\r\n  Neovim>=0.9). It can be customized via `options.custom_commentstring`\r\n  (see |MiniComment.config| for details).\r\n  Current buffer setting can also be set for the particular file type via\r\n `after/ftplugin/<filetype>.lua` with `vim.bo.commentstring = '-- %s'`.\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnyway, nice to see that it works on Nightly. I don't have any further comments on that. I should just switch to nightly as it seems the right way NeoVim community.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What wording would help you in this particular case?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I would just put your previous answer into the readme or help text section you linked. Because it is clear and straight to the point.</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"- Comment structure by default is inferred from 'commentstring': either\n  from current buffer or from locally active tree-sitter language (only on\n  Neovim&gt;=0.9). It can be customized via `options.custom_commentstring`\n  (see |MiniComment.config| for details).\n  Current buffer setting can also be set for the particular file type via\n `after/ftplugin/&lt;filetype&gt;.lua` with `vim.bo.commentstring = '-- %s'`.\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">- Comment structure by default is inferred from 'commentstring': either\n  from current buffer or from locally active tree-sitter language (only on\n  Neovim&gt;=0.9). It can be customized via `options.custom_commentstring`\n  (see |MiniComment.config| for details).\n  Current buffer setting can also be set for the particular file type via\n `after/ftplugin/&lt;filetype&gt;.lua` with `vim.bo.commentstring = '-- %s'`.\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Anyway, nice to see that it works on Nightly. I don't have any further comments on that. I should just switch to nightly as it seems the right way NeoVim community.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "What wording would help you in this particular case?\n\nI would just put your previous answer into the readme or help text section you linked. Because it is clear and straight to the point.\n- Comment structure by default is inferred from 'commentstring': either\n  from current buffer or from locally active tree-sitter language (only on\n  Neovim>=0.9). It can be customized via `options.custom_commentstring`\n  (see |MiniComment.config| for details).\n  Current buffer setting can also be set for the particular file type via\n `after/ftplugin/<filetype>.lua` with `vim.bo.commentstring = '-- %s'`.\n\nAnyway, nice to see that it works on Nightly. I don't have any further comments on that. I should just switch to nightly as it seems the right way NeoVim community.",
